        },
        {
          "id": 2710759845,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Ah, yes it gives some interesting output in my new dissector. Mostly because the spec has more than one piece of information for each bit. I'm not sure if this should be a value_string with two entries or a true_false_string with the description for true and false.\n\nOne example for a bit field called `TX HARQ`:\n```\n0: HARQ TX configuration is accepted or is not modified in the reconfiguration request.\n1: HARQ TX configuration is not accepted. HARQ Process TX and MAX HARQ RE-TX fields are present.\n```\nwhich currently gives:\n```\n{\"Not accepted\", \"Accepted or is not modified in the reconfiguration request\"} both strings contain not\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 4753670,
            "username": "stigbjorlykke",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Stig Bjørlykke",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/905aafc6b50e246885f5ea9273a9dc4f22e2658b71f9a1b551b797082bec3f80?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/stigbjorlykke"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-08-26T18:58:56.065Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-08-26T18:59:46.175Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 410102193,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 21057,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2710935031,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Yes, some fields are just not hard to understand, and don't feel like true/false opposites..",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
